  "text": "Rhiannon is a Welsh goddess, and she also appears as a heroine in the Mabinogion. Her name may follow rigantona, a term that means great queen. She rode a swift white horse and is linked to the horse goddess Epona. Some scholars connect her to the sun. King Pwyll of Dyfed chased her three times and lost each race. She then stopped and told him she had come to seek him. He defeated the rival Gwawl, and they wed. After their son Pryderi vanished, nursemaids spread dog blood on Rhiannon. She took the blame and had to carry visitors on her back. Her son later returned and freed her. Her link to the land ties her to sovereignty.",
